.TH TUIIDE 1 "August 2026" "tuiide 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tuiide \- terminal IDE for C and C++
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tuiide
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ project ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tuiide
is a UTF-8 terminal IDE for Linux/amd64. It provides project browsing,
editing and syntax highlighting, clangd language features, CMake builds,
integrated program execution, and GDB/MI debugging using the Final Cut UI.
The optional project argument must name a directory containing CMakeLists.txt.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h , " " \-\-help
Print command-line help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the program version and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-project " PATH"
Open the CMake project rooted at PATH. A positional project path remains supported.
.TP
.BI \-\-log-file " FILE"
Append timestamped, tab-separated Output and Build events to FILE. Embedded
newlines, carriage returns, tabs, and backslashes are escaped.
.TP
.B \-\-diagnostic
Report detected and missing CMake, clangd, GDB, and native clipboard tools in Output.
.TP
.B \-\-
Stop option processing. Use this before a project path beginning with a dash.
.SH EXTERNAL TOOLS
CMake is required for configure and build operations. clangd supplies C/C++
completion, diagnostics, and navigation. GDB supplies debugging, and clang-format
supplies source formatting. wl-copy/wl-paste, xclip, or xsel enable the native
clipboard; internal and OSC 52 fallbacks remain available without them.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .tuiide-project.json
Per-project build, launch, editor, language-server, and shortcut settings.
.TP
.I BUILD-DIRECTORY/.tuiide-session.json
Open-document and debugger session state.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/tuiide/recent-projects.json
Recent projects. ~/.config is used when XDG_CONFIG_HOME is unset.
.SH KEYBOARD
Press F10 to activate the menu, Alt+K for the command palette, F7 to build,
F6 to run, F5 to start or continue debugging, and Ctrl+D to exit when the
integrated terminal is inactive. The Help menu contains the complete key list.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates normal termination. Status 2 indicates an invalid command line;
other non-zero values indicate startup or runtime failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cmake (1),
.BR clangd (1),
.BR gdb (1),
.BR clang-format (1)
